[temp.deduct.conv]/1: deducing template arguments for a
conversion-function template by matching the template's return
type (P) against the destination conversion-type-id (A).

Phase 4B-2 of the target-type-threading refactor (commit
introducing `deduce_conversion_template` in
`cpp_typecheck_conversions.cpp`) implements this for the
single-template-parameter form `template<class T> operator T()`.

The class `any_t` has a `template <class T> operator T() const`
template conversion operator.  Per [temp.deduct.conv]/1, T is
deduced from the destination type at the point of conversion:

  int  as_int  = a;  // deduces T = int
  long as_long = a;  // deduces T = long

Both `__CPROVER_assert(as_*  == 42, ...)` checks must succeed.
